{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GtP1WsTEs4zoTYAn27PAnG","type":"tool_result","content":"{{- /* executor k8s: a ValidatingAdmissionPolicy on every pod created in the jobs namespace, so a controller bug or a\nstolen controller token cannot widen a job pod. It encodes the pod contract (internal/jobpod, built by\ninternal/executor/kube/pod.go): the ard-job ServiceAccount and no token; no shared process namespace, host\nnamespaces or image pull secrets; only emptyDir volumes and the pod's own Secret (named after the pod, so the App\nSecret and any other Secret are unreachable); containers exactly pre (init), agent and post, pinned by digest; the\nagent mounts no Secret and reads only its model credential; agent and sidecars run as different UIDs. Fails closed.\nThe cluster-scoped names carry the release name, so several instances can coexist. The CEL runs in #321. */ -}}\n{{- if include \"ard-serve.k8s\" . }}\n{{- $name := printf \"%s-jobs\" (include \"ard-serve.name\" .) }}\n{{- $agentUID := int .Values.jobs.agentUID }}\n{{- $sidecarUID := int .Values.jobs.sidecarUID }}\napiVersion: admissionregistration.k8s.io/v1\nkind: ValidatingAdmissionPolicy\nmetadata:\n  name: {{ $name }}\n  labels:\n    {{- include \"ard-serve.labels\" . | nindent 4 }}\nspec:\n  failurePolicy: Fail\n  matchConstraints:\n    resourceRules:\n      - apiGroups: [\"\"]\n        apiVersions: [v1]\n        operations: [CREATE]\n        resources: [pods]\n      - apiGroups: [\"\"]\n        apiVersions: [v1]\n        operations: [UPDATE]\n        resources: [pods/ephemeralcontainers]\n  variables:\n    - name: spec\n      expression: object.spec\n    - name: init\n      expression: \"has(object.spec.initContainers) ? object.spec.initContainers : []\"\n    - name: all\n      expression: object.spec.containers + variables.init\n    - name: volumes\n      expression: \"has(object.spec.volumes) ? object.spec.volumes : []\"\n    - name: podUID\n      expression: >-\n        has(object.spec.securityContext) && has(object.spec.securityContext.runAsUser)\n        ? object.spec.securityContext.runAsUser : -1\n  validations:\n    - expression: \"has(variables.spec.serviceAccountName) && variables.spec.serviceAccountName == 'ard-job'\"\n      message: job pods run as the ard-job ServiceAccount\n    - expression: \"has(variables.spec.automountServiceAccountToken) && variables.spec.automountServiceAccountToken == false\"\n      message: job pods set automountServiceAccountToken false\n    - expression: \"!has(variables.spec.shareProcessNamespace) || variables.spec.shareProcessNamespace == false\"\n      message: job pods do not share a process namespace\n    - expression: >-\n        !(has(variables.spec.hostNetwork) && variables.spec.hostNetwork) &&\n        !(has(variables.spec.hostPID) && variables.spec.hostPID) &&\n        !(has(variables.spec.hostIPC) && variables.spec.hostIPC)\n      message: job pods use no host namespace\n    - expression: \"!has(variables.spec.imagePullSecrets) || size(variables.spec.imagePullSecrets) == 0\"\n      message: job pods have no imagePullSecrets\n    - expression: \"!has(variables.spec.ephemeralContainers) || size(variables.spec.ephemeralContainers) == 0\"\n      message: job pods have no ephemeral containers\n    - expression: \"variables.volumes.all(v, has(v.emptyDir) || has(v.secret))\"\n      message: job pod volumes are emptyDir or Secret only (no hostPath, projected token, CSI or PVC)\n    - expression: \"variables.volumes.all(v, !has(v.secret) || v.secret.secretName == object.metadata.name)\"\n      message: the only Secret a job pod mounts is its own, named after the pod\n    - expression: >-\n        size(variables.init) == 1 && variables.init[0].name == 'pre' &&\n        size(object.spec.containers) == 2 &&\n        object.spec.containers.exists(c, c.name == 'agent') && object.spec.containers.exists(c, c.name == 'post')\n      message: job pods have exactly the init container pre and the containers agent and post\n    - expression: \"variables.all.all(c, has(c.image) && c.image.contains('@sha256:'))\"\n      message: every job pod image is pinned by digest\n    - expression: \"variables.all.all(c, !has(c.envFrom) || size(c.envFrom) == 0)\"\n      message: job pod containers use no envFrom\n    - expression: >-\n        variables.all.all(c, !has(c.env) || c.env.all(e, !has(e.valueFrom) || !has(e.valueFrom.secretKeyRef) ||\n        e.valueFrom.secretKeyRef.name == object.metadata.name))\n      message: secretKeyRef names only the pod's own Secret\n    - expression: >-\n        object.spec.containers.all(c, c.name != 'agent' || !has(c.volumeMounts) ||\n        c.volumeMounts.all(m, variables.volumes.exists(v, v.name == m.name && has(v.emptyDir))))\n      message: the agent container mounts no Secret volume\n    - expression: >-\n        object.spec.containers.all(c, c.name != 'agent' || !has(c.env) ||\n        c.env.all(e, !has(e.valueFrom) || !has(e.valueFrom.secretKeyRef) ||\n        e.valueFrom.secretKeyRef.key in ['ANTHROPIC_API_KEY', 'CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN']))\n      message: the agent container reads only its model credential from the Secret\n    - expression: >-\n        variables.all.all(c,\n        (has(c.securityContext) && has(c.securityContext.runAsUser) ? c.securityContext.runAsUser : variables.podUID)\n        == (c.name == 'agent' ? {{ $agentUID }} : {{ $sidecarUID }}))\n      message: the agent runs as uid {{ $agentUID }} and pre and post as uid {{ $sidecarUID }}\n    - expression: >-\n        has(object.metadata.labels) &&\n        'app.kubernetes.io/part-of' in object.metadata.labels && object.metadata.labels['app.kubernetes.io/part-of'] == 'ard' &&\n        'app.kubernetes.io/component' in object.metadata.labels && object.metadata.labels['app.kubernetes.io/component'] == 'ard-job' &&\n        'app.kubernetes.io/instance' in object.metadata.labels &&\n        object.metadata.labels['app.kubernetes.io/instance'] == '{{ include \"ard-serve.name\" . }}' &&\n        'ard.albertcbrown/repo' in object.metadata.labels && 'ard.albertcbrown/job' in object.metadata.labels &&\n        'ard.albertcbrown/network' in object.metadata.labels &&\n        object.metadata.labels['ard.albertcbrown/network'] in ['true', 'false']\n      message: job pods carry the ard job labels\n---\napiVersion: admissionregistration.k8s.io/v1\nkind: ValidatingAdmissionPolicyBinding\nmetadata:\n  name: {{ $name }}\n  labels:\n    {{- include \"ard-serve.labels\" . | nindent 4 }}\nspec:\n  policyName: {{ $name }}\n  validationActions: [Deny]\n  matchResources:\n    namespaceSelector:\n      matchLabels:\n        kubernetes.io/metadata.name: {{ include \"ard-serve.jobsNamespace\" . }}\n{{- end }}\n1:{{- define \"ard-serve.name\" -}}ard-{{ .Values.instance.name }}{{- end -}}\n2-\n3-{{- define \"ard-serve.labels\" -}}\n4-app.kubernetes.io/name: ard\n5-app.kubernetes.io/instance: {{ include \"ard-serve.name\" . }}\n6-app.kubernetes.io/part-of: ard\n7-{{- end -}}\n--\n24:{{- define \"ard-serve.jobsNamespace\" -}}\n25-{{- .Values.executor.jobsNamespace | default (printf \"ard-jobs-%s\" .Values.instance.name) -}}\n26-{{- end -}}\n27-\n28-{{- /* Every job pod carries these (internal/jobpod: LabelPartOf, LabelComponent, LabelInstance; --k8s-instance is\n29-ard-serve.name). */ -}}\n30-{{- define \"ard-serve.jobSelector\" -}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1019feba-06a1-4cc1-b610-7f34aa3910a8","uuid":"2fa272f3-7f4d-4209-92ab-7b3c35fb9453","timestamp":"2026-11-25T16:31:46.584Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{{- /* executor k8s: a ValidatingAdmissionPolicy on every pod created in the jobs namespace, so a controller bug or a\nstolen controller token cannot widen a job pod. It encodes the pod contract (internal/jobpod, built by\ninternal/executor/kube/pod.go): the ard-job ServiceAccount and no token; no shared process namespace, host\nnamespaces or image pull secrets; only emptyDir volumes and the pod's own Secret (na