{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPyEAS4xEXk6AxUVGaGc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've added the kind end-to-end test and a `kind-e2e` Makefile target, but only part of the plan's scenarios, and none of it has run against a cluster. kind isn't installed here and the test needs one. It compiles and vets with and without the `integration` tag, and the `internal/executor` tests still pass. A human has to run `make kind-e2e` before this counts as acceptance.\n\n**What's in it**\n- **Outer mode:** creates the cluster and registry, builds and pushes the ard and harness images by digest, installs the chart, and scales the Deployment to 0. It then runs each inner test as a pod made from the Deployment's pod template.\n- **Inner mode:** runs a stub agent through the Kubernetes executor against a fixture repo that the harness serves itself.\n- **Scenarios implemented:**\n  - **NetworkPolicy enforcement:** fails loudly if the CNI doesn't block a default-deny probe.\n  - **Admission:** a control pod that follows the contract must be admitted, and eleven mutated pods must be refused.\n  - **Happy path:** checks the result, no token or key visible to the agent, no secret mount, and token revoked after cleanup.\n  - **ReadWriteOncePod:** a second pod on the claim must stay Pending, and if it doesn't the test records that and doesn't fail.\n\n**Open issues**\n- **Reduced scope:**\n  - **Scenarios not built:** the wrong-key, early-pull, missing-result, oversize, controller-restart, egress and ingress scenarios.\n  - **Close-out commit:** not covered. The happy path checks the pulled result, not a commit.\n  - **Token revocation:** only after cleanup, not after `pre`.\n- **Versions not pinned:**\n  - **No `deploy/kind-up.sh`:** `deploy/` is protected, so the test creates the cluster itself.\n  - **Pins left open:** I didn't use the network, so the kind version, node image and `registry:2` tag are unpinned. `ARD_KIND_NODE_IMAGE` overrides the node image.\n- **First-run risks:**\n  - **containerd config:** it uses `certs.d/hosts.toml`, so image pulls from `localhost:5001` fail if the pinned kind's containerd also needs `config_path` patched in.\n  - **Admission messages:** the cases assume the refusal text names the policy.\n- **CI:** a human still needs to add the workflow under `.github/`.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/321/worker-engineer.md`; the test code is in `internal/executor/kube/e2e/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1684,"cache_read_input_tokens":85500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1684},"output_tokens":749,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1019feba-06a1-4cc1-b610-7f34aa3910a8","uuid":"d15e9cdb-b962-4c18-b7a1-6809bafa16d4","timestamp":"2026-11-25T16:34:52.200Z","request_id":"req_011ChPyEAHdHXYwvaCgtRz54"}
